[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]High-Performance, Secure, and Universal Player Data Synchronization[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

MC Data Bridge is a robust, high-performance hybrid synchronization suite for [B]Paper/Spigot[/B], [B]Folia[/B], [B]BungeeCord[/B], and [B]Velocity[/B]. Designed for high-traffic production networks, it ensures a seamless cross-server experience by synchronizing health, hunger, experience, inventories, ender chests, advancements, and more with zero lag and industrial-grade security.

[SIZE=5]► Key Features[/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Universal Hybrid Plugin:[/B] A single JAR file detects its environment and activates correct logic for Spigot, Paper, Folia, BungeeCord, or Velocity.
[*][B]Full Vanilla Player Statistics Sync:[/B] A dynamic, version-independent sync loop that replicates all vanilla stats (e.g., mined blocks, crafted items, entity kills) across servers, with automatic state cleanup and version resilience.
[*][B]Companion & Pet Synchronization:[/B] Synchronizes wolves, cats, parrots, and other pets. Saves shoulder-perched states, custom names, ownership, health, and NBT metadata. Offers three modes: `follow`, `return`, and `untracked`.
[*][B]Relational Schema Normalization:[/B] Introduces component tables (`databridge_inventories`, `databridge_statistics`, `databridge_metadata`, `databridge_companions`) to eliminate write-amplification and database locks.
[*][B]Binary NBT Serialization:[/B] Adds a compressed binary serialization format (`serialization-format: binary`) to minimize database footprint, I/O bandwidth, and CPU overhead.
[*][B]Production Security Hardening:[/B] Fails-strict validation prevents startup if the default cryptographic seed is detected, guarding against unauthorized joins. Sanitized whitelisting secures all database DDL commands.
[*][B]Embedded Prometheus Exporter:[/B] Provides an HTTP `/metrics` endpoint to monitor HikariCP connection pools, transaction latencies, active queries, and cache efficiency.
[*][B]SHA-256 Data Integrity:[/B] Every data packet is verified with a SHA-256 checksum and a server-side salt, preventing manual database tampering or corruption.
[*][B]Industrial Identity Protection:[/B] Secure tracking of [I]last_known_name[/I] and identity hashes allows for reliable UUID change detection and prevention of identity hijacking in hybrid environments.
[*][B]Zero-Tick Identity Verification:[/B] Database locks and identity checks are performed during the [I]AsyncPlayerPreLoginEvent[/I], ensuring that player state is verified and ready before they even reach the server's "Join" state.
[*][B]Regionalized Folia Support:[/B] Fully compatible with Folia's regionalized threading, ensuring safe data handling on modern multi-threaded server clusters.
[*][B]Interactive Inventory & Ender Chest Inspector (`invsee` / `endersee`):[/B] Inspect offline or cross-server player inventories with default safe read-only viewing ([I]Left-Click[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect[/I]) and permission-gated interactive edit mode ([I]Right-Click[/I] or [I]--edit[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I]) with automatic database synchronization.
[*][B]Full Command Tab Completion:[/B] Comprehensive auto-completion for subcommands, player names, view options, and flags.
[*][B]Administrative Inspector GUI:[/B] Visual tools for administrators to inspect player data (inventory, stats, PDC) directly from the database without the player needing to be online.
[*][B]Proxy-Orchestrated Saves:[/B] The proxy (Bungee/Velocity) ensures data is flushed and verified before a player connects to the destination server, eliminating race conditions.
[*][B]Granular Sync Control:[/B] Per-component toggles in the config:
[LIST]
[*]Health (Attribute-aware)
[*]Food Level, Saturation, & [B]Exhaustion[/B]
[*]Experience & Levels
[*]Inventories & Armor
[*]Active Potion Effects
[*]Ender Chests
[*]Advancements & Recipes
[*]Statistics (Dynamic Vanilla Statistics)
[*]Persistent Data Container (PDC)
[*]Flight & Gamemode Status
[*]Companions & Pets
[*][B]Map Items & Canvas Sync[/B] (Cross-server map canvas sync via [CODE]sync-data.maps: true[/CODE] with optional map locking via [CODE]maps.lock-global-maps: true[/CODE]. Defaults: [CODE]sync-data.maps: false[/CODE] and [CODE]maps.lock-global-maps: false[/CODE] for vanilla Fog of War map tracking)
[*][B]Separate Gamemode Inventories[/B] (Opt-in separate profiles for Survival, Creative, Adventure, Spectator)
[/LIST]
[*][B]Flexible Storage:[/B] Support for high-performance MySQL/MariaDB clusters or local SQLite databases.
[*][B]Server/World Blacklist:[/B] Prevent synchronization on specific servers or worlds.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Installation[/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*][B]Deploy the JAR:[/B] Place the same `mc-data-bridge-*.jar` file into the `plugins/` folder of all your Minecraft servers AND your BungeeCord/Velocity proxy.
[*][B]Initial Setup:[/B] Start your servers to generate the default configuration.
[*][B]Configure Database:[/B] Edit `plugins/mc-data-bridge/config.yml` on each server. Set your database credentials, choose your `serialization-format`, and ensure each server has a unique `server-id`.
[*][B]Set Security Seed:[/B] Change the `security.seed` in your config to a long, random string. This is mandatory for the plugin to start.
[*][B]Restart & Sync:[/B] Restart all components. Your data is now securely linked!
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Commands & Permissions[/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge inspect <player> [inventory|enderchest] [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens GUI to view or edit saved player data/inventory.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge invsee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens saved player inventory view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge endersee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens saved player ender chest view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge migrate <src> <dest>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Securely move data between two identities.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Manually release a stuck data lock.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge reload[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Reloads the configuration and DB pool.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[/LIST]

[B]Proxy Commands:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B] (Bungee/Velocity): Releases a lock across the network.
[*][B]/databridge forceunlock <player>[/B] (Bungee/Velocity): Relays a signal to the backend server to drop the lock immediately.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Permission Nodes:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]databridge.inspect[/B]: Permission to view player data, inventories, and ender chests in safe read-only mode.
[*][B]databridge.inspect.edit[/B]: Elevated permission required to interactively edit inventories and ender chests via [I]--edit[/I] or Right-Click.
[*][B]databridge.admin[/B]: Master administrative access for all commands and functions.
[/LIST]

